{"reference":"Revelation 14","book":"Revelation","chapter":14,"status":"pending","sections":[{"kind":"interpretive_questions","title":"The 144,000 and endurance","blocks":[{"id":"block_1","text":"The 144,000 appear here with the Lamb and are marked by his and his Father’s names. Their earlier numbering and sealing from Israel’s tribes has led to differing views about how they relate to the multitude elsewhere in the book. What is clear in this chapter is the contrast between those identified with the Lamb and those marked by the beast. Verse 12 directs the saints toward endurance, obedience, and faithfulness; Revelation’s scenes of divine judgment are not a mandate for its hearers to carry out religious violence.","verse_refs":["Revelation 14:1-5","Revelation 14:12"],"provenance_refs":["reader_path_revelation_014_55140a924e49af459cc3369d"],"confidence":"medium","interpretation_level":"disputed"}]},{"kind":"interpretive_questions","title":"Harvest and winepress imagery","blocks":[{"id":"block_2","text":"The harvest and winepress scenes use prophetic imagery that plausibly recalls Joel, while also drawing together material from more than one prophetic source. They should therefore be read as cumulative allusions rather than as a direct quotation of a single earlier passage. This helps account for the chapter’s compressed, symbolic portrayal of judgment through reaping grapes and treading a winepress.","verse_refs":["Revelation 14:14-20"],"provenance_refs":["reader_path_revelation_014_1bf46a3b7bf2c275a0d49b12"],"confidence":"medium","interpretation_level":"disputed"}]},{"kind":"surrounding_passages","title":"Reading Revelation as a whole","blocks":[{"id":"block_3","text":"Across Revelation, imagery from Israel’s Scriptures is repeatedly reworked, especially material associated with Daniel, Ezekiel, Isaiah, Exodus, Zechariah, Genesis, and Psalms. The book also organizes major judgment visions through sequences of seven seals, seven trumpets, and seven bowls, with interludes and recurring motifs. These broader patterns help situate chapter 14 within Revelation’s larger symbolic presentation.","verse_refs":["Revelation 10:1-11","Revelation 11:1-19","Revelation 12:1-17","Revelation 13:1-18","Revelation 15:1-8","Revelation 16:1-21","Revelation 17:1-18","Revelation 18:1-24","Revelation 19:1-21","Revelation 1:1-20","Revelation 20:1-15","Revelation 21:1-27","Revelation 22:1-21","Revelation 2:1-29","Revelation 3:1-22","Revelation 4:1-11","Revelation 5:1-14","Revelation 6:1-17","Revelation 7:1-17","Revelation 8:1-13","Revelation 9:1-21"],"provenance_refs":["reader_path_revelation_014_436bc29e9ce9869e7d431f1f"],"confidence":"high","interpretation_level":"disputed"}]}],"generated_metadata":null}